<article class="env-lemma" id="36B448">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/36B448">Lemma <span data-tag="36B448">2.4.3.1</span>.</a> Let $A \subseteq B$ be an inclusion of simplicial sets. Then the inclusion </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\{ 1\}  \star B) \coprod _{ \{ 1\}  \star A } (\Delta ^1 \star A ) \subseteq \Delta ^1 \star B \]
</div>
  <p> is inner anodyne. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Working by transfinite induction, we may reduce to the case where $B$ is obtained from $A$ by adjoining a single non-degenerate simplex, and therefore to the universal case $B = \Delta ^ n$, $A = \bd \Delta ^ n$. Now the inclusion in question is isomorphic to $\Lambda ^{n+2}_{1} \subseteq \Delta ^{n+2}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>